SOAPBOX: Conditions terrible from this little pistols perspective. Quite
SOAPBOX: a few stations I normally worked just CQd in my face. Deep QSB
SOAPBOX: on some signals. Contacts were slow going. After the first night
SOAPBOX: and Saturday B4 sunrise I should have been over 200 plus Qs. I
SOAPBOX: barely managed to hit 155 Qs. Saturday night was a real struggle
SOAPBOX: as the snow storm changed over to an ice storm and the SWR kept
SOAPBOX: fluctuating and I had to continuously retune the MFJ tuner. It
SOAPBOX: was a struggle to make the next 67 Qs to put me a bit over 200 Qs.
SOAPBOX: QRTd at 05:37utc Sunday and called it a contest. Woke up Sunday
SOAPBOX: morning to half inch plus of ice on all the antennas, and still
SOAPBOX: sleeting and freezing rain coming down. 160 inverted L wire
SOAPBOX: stretched and loaded down to the ground with half inch or more of
SOAPBOX: ice coating the 110' of wire. Still freezing rain and sleet coming
SOAPBOX: down as I type this. Looks like I'll be qrt from 160 till spring
SOAPBOX: rolls around.
SOAPBOX: 73, Gene N9TF
SOAPBOX: K3S 100 watts to inverted L 22' to knee 110' horizontal traveling
SOAPBOX: west.
